From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jbevan <jbevan@bu.edu>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:41:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Client: headless tool mode (-mtool) and non-interactive
 login (--noprompt)

A display module with no UI for programs that play: the client reads one
command per line on stdin (walk, pathfind, custom commands, store actions,
look, rest, chat, option, queries for the map, inventory, flags, ...) and
reports what happens as JSON lines on stdout (messages, popups, the full-level
map with attributes, monster and item lists, store contents, position and
level changes, confirm prompts). The full list of events and commands is at
the top of src/client/c-tool.c.

Also: --noprompt logs in without the interactive prompts, --birth creates the
character without the birth menus, --visuals FILE uploads a glyph table, and
--hpwarn sets the time-bubble warning. The tool client tracks the server's
silent store exit and refuses store commands and redraws outside a store.

New files src/client/c-tool.c and main-tool.c (the -mtool module); hooks in
c-init.c, c-birth.c, c-util.c, c-xtra2.c, c-files.c, c-variable.c, client.c,
net-client.c, c-externs.h and src/client/Makefile.am.
